    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218">

                <pb facs="0705" n="691" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg691"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hall, district attorney, to Mr. Clayton Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Southern District of New York,
                            United States District Attorney’s Office</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1850-05-25T15:00:00-04:56"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">May</hi> 25, 1850—half-past 3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                <p><seg type="margin">[666]</seg>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Spanish consul is in my office, and,
                    upon *an affidavit made by him, I have just issued a warrant for the arrest of
                    M. T. Tolon.</p>
                <p>Your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. PRESCOTT HALL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States
                            Attorney.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S.—Will the President authorize me to act under the 8th section, in order
                        to seize and detain munitions of war intended to be used in aid of the Cuban
                        expedition?</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
